{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md | sed -n '74,126p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go | sed -n '1070,1125p'\"","aggregated_output":"    74\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n    75\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\n    76\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n    77\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n    78\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n    79\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n    80\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n    81\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/help_catalog.go\n    82\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_reap_test.go\n    83\t- modified: POSE.md\n    84\t- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n    85\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n    86\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t### Delivery targets\n    90\t\n    91\t- capability:review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n    92\t\n    93\t\n    94\t### API/contract changes\n    95\t`pose delegate cancel` releases a stalled attempt that has no run, recording a failed run and its receipt. Brief template `review-brief/10`. The run record's `safety.limitations` names the processes the dispatch ended after the adapter.\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t### Data/storage changes\n    99\tA released attempt gets an ordinary failed run record and attempt receipt; no schema changes.\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t### Technical risks\n   103\tThe leftover processes are found by the `POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT=<checkout>` entry of their environment, which every process of the run inherits; a process that clears its environment escapes, and the existing cleanup inventory still fails that run (L1). Reading another process's environment needs Linux and the same user; elsewhere the group kill stays the only termination (L2).\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t## 4. Tasks\n   107\t\n   108\t### Planning\n   109\t- [ ] Confirm the cause against the current engine before starting.\n   110\t\n   111\t### Implementation\n   112\t- [ ] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n   113\t\n   114\t### Validation\n   115\t- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n   116\t\n   117\t## 5. Decisions\n   118\t\n   119\t### Decision D1\n   120\t- Basis: R1, R2\n   121\tLeftover processes are identified by the sealed-checkout entry the dispatch already sets in the run's environment, not by process group or session: adapters such as `codex exec` run each command in a session of its own, which the group kill misses, and the entry names this run's checkout only.\n   122\t\n   123\t### Decision D2\n   124\t- Basis: R5\n   125\tAn abandoned attempt is closed by the records a failed run writes (a run record and its receipt), released only when its marker is stalled and its owner proven dead. Nothing is deleted from the ledger, and older engines read the result as an ordinary failed run.\n   126\t\n  1070\t\t\t\trun.Provenance.ExecutionState = \"started\"\n  1071\t\t\t}\n  1072\t\t}\n  1073\t\tif useShim && safety != nil {\n  1074\t\t\t// With the shim the run's leftovers are its subtree, not an\n  1075\t\t\t// environment match (review round 9, N1).\n  1076\t\t\tfor i, limit := range safety.Limitations {\n  1077\t\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(limit, \"no memory/CPU quota;\") {\n  1078\t\t\t\t\tsafety.Limitations[i] = \"no memory/CPU quota; the review run shim ends every process left in the run's subtree, including one in its own session\"\n  1079\t\t\t\t}\n  1080\t\t\t}\n  1081\t\t}\n  1082\t\tif useShim {\n  1083\t\t\t_ = shimWrite.Close()\n  1084\t\t\t<-shimReportDone\n  1085\t\t\t_ = shimRead.Close()\n  1086\t\t}\n  1087\t\tterminationErr = killProcessGroup(cmd)\n  1088\t\t// A command the reviewer left running in a session of its own escapes the\n  1089\t\t// group kill; it is ended here, before the cleanup inventory reads the\n  1090\t\t// directories it may still write (spec\n  1091\t\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R1, R2).\n  1092\t\t// The environment entry is the reviewer's to set, so it is searched only\n  1093\t\t// without the shim, whose subtree is the run's by construction (review\n  1094\t\t// round 8, N1).\n  1095\t\tvar reaped []string\n  1096\t\tvar opaque int\n  1097\t\tvar reapErr error\n  1098\t\tif !useShim {\n  1099\t\t\treaped, opaque, reapErr = reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(worktree, opaqueBaseline)\n  1100\t\t\tif reapErr != nil {\n  1101\t\t\t\tterminationErr = errors.Join(terminationErr, reapErr)\n  1102\t\t\t}\n  1103\t\t}\n  1104\t\tif useShim && cmd.ProcessState != nil {\n  1105\t\t\tif report, err := parseReviewShimReport(shimReport); err != nil {\n  1106\t\t\t\tterminationErr = errors.Join(terminationErr, err)\n  1107\t\t\t} else {\n  1108\t\t\t\tfor _, pid := range report.Ended {\n  1109\t\t\t\t\treaped = append(reaped, pid+\" (orphaned)\")\n  1110\t\t\t\t}\n  1111\t\t\t\tif more := report.EndedTotal - len(report.Ended); more > 0 {\n  1112\t\t\t\t\treaped = append(reaped, fmt.Sprintf(\"and %d more (orphaned)\", more))\n  1113\t\t\t\t}\n  1114\t\t\t\tif report.Error != \"\" {\n  1115\t\t\t\t\tterminationErr = errors.Join(terminationErr, errors.New(report.Error))\n  1116\t\t\t\t}\n  1117\t\t\t}\n  1118\t\t}\n  1119\t\tif len(reaped) > 0 && safety != nil {\n  1120\t\t\tsafety.Limitations = append(safety.Limitations, \"ended \"+fmt.Sprint(len(reaped))+\" process(es) the run left running: \"+strings.Join(reaped, \", \"))\n  1121\t\t}\n  1122\t\tif opaque > 0 && reapErr == nil && safety != nil {\n  1123\t\t\tsafety.Limitations = append(safety.Limitations, fmt.Sprint(opaque)+\" process(es) of this user that existed before the run could not be inspected for its environment entry\")\n  1124\t\t}\n  1125\t\tterminationFailed = terminationErr != nil\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
