{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_DRAFT' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 147,\n      \"summary\": \"The shim treats every visible /proc entry whose stat cannot be read as a run child before checking ownership or parent PID. On procfs configured with hidepid=1, unrelated users'\"' processes can be visible but unreadable, so a clean review can hit the reaper timeout, retain runtime resources, and fail instead of reaching inventory. Filter processes that can be proven unrelated and scope uncertainty to possible run children.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 190,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"orphanReservations uses unbounded os.ReadDir calls for the attempt root and every nested directory. Its 32 MiB file-byte budget does not bound directory entry counts or empty directories, and pose delegate ls runs this scan. Large local attempt trees can consume excessive memory and delay listing or cancellation.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Use bounded directory and record enumeration for orphan reservations and return a typed loss when the inventory exceeds its limit.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1104,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The shim records a PID before confirming SIGKILL succeeded; the dispatcher then labels every reported PID as ended. It joins report.Error into a local error but records only the generic 'process group termination failed' failure, so an unkillable process can be reported as ended while the specific PID and cause are lost.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Persist bounded per-process termination results and distinguish attempted from confirmed-reaped PIDs in the run record.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 103,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The spec's Technical risks text and D1 at line 121 still describe sealed-checkout environment matching as the normal Linux design and say clearing the environment escapes; the standard CLI now uses the run shim subtree. The fallback-only scope also remains unstated in the Linux helper comment at pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:10-12.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Update the spec risk and D1 plus the helper comment to distinguish the default Linux shim, the shimless embedder fallback, and non-Linux process-group behavior.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:974-985,1087-1100; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go:98-134\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-N4\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:49-63; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go:194-228\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R9-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"POSE.md:1078; locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1075; pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1065; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1073-1079\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R9-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim.go:47-61; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1053-1058; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_test.go:12-24\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R9-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:122-178\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept the brief-listed pose-mcp CLI, dispatch, shim/reaper, active marker, attempt ledger/release, review brief and digest tests, plus English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. Traced normal exit, timeout, dispatcher death, session-escaping descendants, attempt publication/release races, receipts, listing, bounded diagnostics, compatibility, and platform-specific behavior.\\\"\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_DRAFT\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_DRAFT' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go\",\n      \"line\": 147,\n      \"summary\": \"The shim treats every visible /proc entry whose stat cannot be read as a run child before checking ownership or parent PID. On procfs configured with hidepid=1, unrelated users'\"' processes can be visible but unreadable, so a clean review can hit the reaper timeout, retain runtime resources, and fail instead of reaching inventory. Filter processes that can be proven unrelated and scope uncertainty to possible run children.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 190,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"orphanReservations uses unbounded os.ReadDir calls for the attempt root and every nested directory. Its 32 MiB file-byte budget does not bound directory entry counts or empty directories, and pose delegate ls runs this scan. Large local attempt trees can consume excessive memory and delay listing or cancellation.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Use bounded directory and record enumeration for orphan reservations and return a typed loss when the inventory exceeds its limit.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1104,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The shim records a PID before confirming SIGKILL succeeded; the dispatcher then labels every reported PID as ended. It joins report.Error into a local error but records only the generic 'process group termination failed' failure, so an unkillable process can be reported as ended while the specific PID and cause are lost.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Persist bounded per-process termination results and distinguish attempted from confirmed-reaped PIDs in the run record.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N4\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"follow-up\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\".pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 103,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The spec's Technical risks text and D1 at line 121 still describe sealed-checkout environment matching as the normal Linux design and say clearing the environment escapes; the standard CLI now uses the run shim subtree. The fallback-only scope also remains unstated in the Linux helper comment at pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:10-12.\\\",\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"Update the spec risk and D1 plus the helper comment to distinguish the default Linux shim, the shimless embedder fallback, and non-Linux process-group behavior.\\\",\n      \\\"owner\\\": \\\"@pose-maintainers\\\",\n      \\\"review_by\\\": \\\"2026-12-24\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"prior_findings\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:974-985,1087-1100; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go:98-134\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R8-N4\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:49-63; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go:194-228\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R9-N1\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"POSE.md:1078; locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1075; pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1065; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1073-1079\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R9-N2\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim.go:47-61; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1053-1058; pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_test.go:12-24\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"R9-N3\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"fixed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:122-178\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"sweep\\\": \\\"Swept the brief-listed pose-mcp CLI, dispatch, shim/reaper, active marker, attempt ledger/release, review brief and digest tests, plus English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. Traced normal exit, timeout, dispatcher death, session-escaping descendants, attempt publication/release races, receipts, listing, bounded diagnostics, compatibility, and platform-specific behavior.\\\"\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_DRAFT\n'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
